<decision #track.bind-eidolon-ai-workflow-to-depa-flows-core.contract-boundary apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BJ>
  Which workflow semantics may remain locally defined in Eidolon?
  </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BJ>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BK>
    Only Eidolon-owned additive facts and compatibility projections.
    </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BK>
    <decision-text ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BM>
    Kinds, substrates, definition bindings, reuse policies and resource-ref semantics come from depa-flows; Eidolon owns its data-subgraph declaration, roots and runtime fact references.
    </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BM>
    <rationale ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BN>
    This preserves fact authority without erasing host-specific integration contracts.
    </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BN>
    <evidence ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BP>
    Mission depa-flows-authority and runtime-reuse decisions.
    </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BP>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.bind-eidolon-ai-workflow-to-depa-flows-core.source-only-loader apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BQ>
  Should the core binding loader read host files?
  </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BQ>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BR>
    No.
    </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BR>
    <decision-text ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BS>
    The core binding exposes a named-source loader; filesystem and resource-store effects are injected by the later authoring workspace track.
    </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BS>
    <rationale ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BT>
    This keeps parsing deterministic and avoids giving CLI or TUI a private filesystem authority.
    </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BT>
    <evidence ?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BV>
    Mission shared-authoring-adapter decision and depa-flows source-loader API.
    </?01M05F1PPM0ADQS94PTKGN16BV>
  )>
)>
